course: dictionary
lesson: 10254
title: Tonal: sound and shade
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and tonal is one of them. Its main meaning is to do with tone: the sound, pitch or quality of something. Pitch means how high or low a sound is. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Mandarin is a tonal language: the same sounds with different pitch patterns make different words.» The clue is in the sentence: tonal is about sound, and the pitch changes the meaning of a word.
explain: Tonal also appears in other subjects. In art, it is about light and dark shades of a colour. In music, it is about pitch and keys. Ask yourself which subject the text is about, and that will show you which meaning fits.
fact: Tonal means to do with tone: the sound, pitch or quality of something.
fact: A tonal language uses the rise and fall of the voice to change the meaning of a word.
fact: Mandarin Chinese is a tonal language: the same sounds with different pitch patterns make different words.
fact: Mandarin has four main tones and a neutral tone.
fact: In art, tonal means to do with light and dark shades of a colour.
exercise: «Mandarin is a tonal language: the same sounds with different pitch patterns make different words.» What does tonal mean in this sentence? | To do with the sea | *To do with sound and pitch | To do with cooking food | To do with light and dark shades
exercise: In art, what does tonal mean? | To do with how high or low a sound is | To do with using only one brush | *To do with light and dark shades of a colour | To do with the size of a painting
exercise: In a tonal language, what changes the meaning of a word? | *The rise and fall of the voice | The colour of the page | The length of the sentence | The number of letters
test: Which subject uses tonal to mean light and dark shades? | Music | Geography | Maths | *Art
test: A tonal language uses what to change the meaning of a word? | Spelling | *Pitch, the rise and fall of the voice | The size of the letters
exam: In a music lesson about keys, what does tonal most likely mean? | To do with the weather | To do with shades of light | *To do with pitch and sound | To do with tall buildings
